    <Placemark>
      <name>Barqa (ברקת)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Barqa (ברקת)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 3: Approximate Village / Spring Area (&lt; 500m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5 (Pages 68)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>The site shows evidence of rainwater storage in soft chalk bedrock, indicating the use of rock-cut cisterns during the Early Bronze Age.</p>]]></description>
