    <Placemark>
      <name>Ein Qadis (עין קדיס)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Ein Qadis (עין קדיס)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 3: Approximate Village / Spring Area (&lt; 500m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.9 (Pages 59)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A permanent spring in the Western Negev Highlands, serving as a crucial water source around which Early Bronze Age settlements were concentrated.</p>]]></description>
