    <Placemark>
      <name>Jawa (ג&apos;ווה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Jawa (ג&apos;ווה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.12 (Pages 65, 66)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Three water collection systems and two modified natural pools (P3, P4) with a total capacity of 1800 cubic meters. The system involved diverting water from Wadi Rajil with a diversion dam and channels to fill the pools, dated to the Early Bronze Age.</p>]]></description>
