    <Placemark>
      <name>Khirbet Zeiraqoun (חירבת זירקון)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Zeiraqoun (חירבת זירקון)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Tunnel Shaft</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.3 (Pages 56, 57)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Three stepped shafts were excavated, leading to a groundwater level approximately 60m deep. One shaft is 100m long, reaching the bottom of Wadi Shallala. Horizontal tunnels and connecting stepped tunnels were proposed to bring water into the city, dated to EB 2-3.</p>]]></description>
