    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Dalit (תל דלית)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Dalit (תל דלית)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.16 (Pages 68, 69, 70)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A fortified Early Bronze Age settlement with several rock-cut cisterns in soft chalk bedrock, designed to collect rainwater. One examined cistern was irregular, 2.2m deep to the chamber, with a rectangular chamber 2.6x2.0m, showing no signs of plaster due to the impermeable chalk. Shallow wells in nearby wadis likely supplemented water supply during peacetime.</p>]]></description>
