    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Megiddo (תל מגידו)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Megiddo (תל מגידו)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Ancient City Water System</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jezreel Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5 (Pages 71)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Despite massive city walls, an Early Bronze Age water system was likely present, possibly a depression in the northern part of the tel, though specific details are scarce due to later archaeological layers.</p>]]></description>
