    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Yarmut (תל ירמות)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Yarmut (תל ירמות)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5 (Pages 71)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Although no formal water system has been discovered for the Early Bronze Age, a clear topographical depression at the lowest point of the 150-dunam city likely served to collect runoff water.</p>]]></description>
