    <Placemark>
      <name>Tepe Gawra (טפה גאורה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tepe Gawra (טפה גאורה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Mesopotamia</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.4 (Pages 57)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Two wells were found. The older well (Layer VIIIb, Late Uruk/EB) was 2.8m in diameter, excavated to 24m, plastered with mud, and featured steps, connected to a bitumen-lined drainage channel. A second well (Layer VI, early 3rd millennium BCE) also had a drainage channel leading to it.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Early_Bronze</styleUrl>
